hadiths[87]{hadithnumber,text}:
"23182","Sufyan narrated to us from Abu Hazim from Sahl from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: I was sent, I and the Hour, like this from this."
"23183","Sufyan narrated to us from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The place of a whip in Paradise is better than the world and what is in it."
"23184","Sufyan narrated to us: Abu Hazim narrated to us, saying: I heard Sahl ibn Sa'd say: I was among the people when a woman entered and said: O Messenger of Allah, she has given herself to you, so see your opinion concerning her; then a man said: Marry her to me; and he did not answer him until she stood a third time; then he said to him: Have you anything? He said: No; he said: Go and seek; he said: I found nothing; he said: Then go and seek even an iron ring; he said: I found not even an iron ring; he said: Have you anything of the Qur'an with you? He said: Yes, such-and-such chapter and such-and-such chapter; he said: I have married her to you for what you have of the Qur'an."
"23185","Sufyan narrated to us from Abu Hazim from Sahl: With what was the wound of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, treated? He said: Ali would bring water in his shield and Fatimah would wash the blood from his face, and he took a mat, burned it, and stuffed his wound with it."
"23186","Sufyan narrated to us from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd who said: It was of the tamarisk of the thicket, meaning the pulpit of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"23187","Sufyan narrated to us from Abu Hazim: He heard Sahl ibn Sa'd from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever is prompted by anything in his prayer, let him say: Glory be to Allah; clapping is only for women and glorifying is for men."
"23188","Sufyan narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Sahl ibn Sa'd: A man peeped through a hole into the chamber of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with an iron spike with which he scratched his head; then he said: Had I known you were watching, I would have stabbed your eye with it; seeking permission was only made on account of sight."
"23189","Sufyan narrated to us from al-Zuhri: He heard Sahl ibn Sa'd: He witnessed the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with the two mutual invokers of curse; then they invoked curse in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and I was fifteen years old; he said: O Messenger of Allah, if I keep her I have lied about her; he said: Then she gave birth to one he disliked."
"23190","Waki' narrated to us: Jarir ibn Hazim and Sufyan narrated to us from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: People remain in good so long as they hasten breaking the fast."
"23191","Waki' narrated to us: Rabi'ah ibn Uthman al-Taymi narrated to us from Imran ibn Abi Anas from Sahl ibn Sa'd who said: Two men differed in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, over the mosque founded on piety; then one of them said: It is the mosque of the Messenger; and the other said: It is the mosque of Quba; then they came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and asked him; then he said: It is this mosque of mine."
"23192","Ya'qub narrated to us: My father narrated to us from Ibn Ishaq: Abu Hazim al-A'war, freedman of al-Aswad ibn Sufyan al-Makhzumi, narrated to me from Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi of Banu Amr concerning a dispute, and he mentioned the hadith - [source testimony abbreviated]."
"23193","Yazid narrated to us: al-Mas'udi told us from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd who said: There was a matter among some of the Ansar, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went to them to make peace between them; then prayer came, and Bilal came to Abu Bakr and said: O Abu Bakr, prayer has come, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, is not here; so shall I call and establish, and you advance and pray? He said: Do what you wish; then Abu Bakr advanced and began the prayer, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came, and the people clapped for Abu Bakr; then Abu Bakr went to step aside, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gestured to him: your place; then Abu Bakr stepped back, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, advanced and prayed; then when he finished the prayer he said: O Abu Bakr, what kept you from standing firm? He said: It was not for the son of Abu Quhafah to advance before the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him; he said: Then why did you clap? They said: To inform Abu Bakr; he said: Clapping is for women and glorifying is for men."
"23194","Anas ibn Iyad narrated to us: Abu Hazim narrated to me - I know him only from Sahl ibn Sa'd - who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Beware minor sins, like a people camping in a valley bottom: this brings a stick and this brings a stick until they baked their bread; and minor sins, when their doer is seized by them, destroy him."
"23195","And Abu Hazim said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said - Abu Damrah said: I know him only from Sahl ibn Sa'd who said: My likeness and the Hour are like these two, and he separated between his middle finger and the one next to the thumb."
"23196","Then he said: My likeness and the Hour are like two racehorses."
"23197","Then he said: My likeness and the Hour are like a man whom his people sent as a scout; when he feared to be overtaken, he waved his garment: You are come, you are come; then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, says: I am that."
"23198","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us from Abu Hazim, saying: I heard Sahl ibn Sa'd say: Men would pray with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, tying their waist-wrappers around their necks like children; then it was said to women: Do not raise your heads until the men sit upright."
"23199","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Ma'mar told us from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sa'd: Uhud shook with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman upon it; then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Be firm, Uhud; upon you is but a prophet, a truthful one, and two martyrs."
"23200","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us: Ayyash, meaning Ibn Uqbah, narrated to us: Yahya ibn Maymun narrated to me - and Abu al-Husayn Zayd ibn al-Hubab said: Ayyash, meaning Ibn Uqbah, narrated to me, saying: Yahya ibn Maymun narrated to me - the meaning: Sahl ibn Sa'd stopped upon us and said: Sahl said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever sits in the mosque awaiting prayer is in prayer."
"23201","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman, meaning Ibn Abd Allah ibn Dinar, narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: There was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a man in one of his expeditions, and he fought valiantly, so the Muslims were amazed at his fighting. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As for him, he is among the people of Hellfire. We said: In the cause of Allah, alongside the Messenger of Allah? Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: The man went out, and when his wounds became severe he placed the tip of his sword between his breasts, then leaned upon it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was approached and it was said to him: The man about whom you said what you said, I saw him writhing with the sword among his ribs. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man may do the deeds of the people of Paradise as it appears to people, yet he is among the people of Hellfire, and he may do the deeds of the people of Hellfire as it appears to people, yet he is among the people of Paradise."
"23202","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman, meaning Ibn Abd Allah ibn Dinar, narrated to us: Abu Hazim narrated to us, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, that it was said to him: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) see fine white flour with his own eyes before his death, meaning huwwara? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never saw fine flour with his own eyes until he met Allah, Mighty and Majestic. It was said to him: Did you have sieves in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: We had no sieves. It was said to him: How did you deal with barley? He said: We would blow on it, and whatever flew off would fly away."
"23203","Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, from his father, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at al-Khandaq, while they were digging and we were carrying the dust upon our shoulders. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, there is no life but the life of the Hereafter, so forgive the Muhajirun and the Ansar."
"23204","Affan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us: Abu Hazim narrated to us, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: There was fighting between Banu Amr ibn Awf, and it reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he went to them after Zuhr to make peace between them. He said: O Bilal, if the prayer comes and I have not come, then order Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer. He said: When Asr came, Bilal called the iqamah for prayer, then ordered Abu Bakr, so he stepped forward with them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came after Abu Bakr had entered the prayer. When they saw him they clapped, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came parting the people until he stood behind Abu Bakr. He said: Abu Bakr, when he entered prayer, would not turn around, but when he saw the clapping would not stop, he turned and saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) behind him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gestured to him with his hand to go ahead. Abu Bakr stood a while, then praised Allah for that, then walked backwards. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stepped forward and prayed with the people. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished his prayer, he said: O Abu Bakr, what prevented you, when I gestured to you, from going ahead? Abu Bakr said: It was not for Ibn Abi Quhafah to lead the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in prayer. He said to the people: If something befalls you in your prayer, let the men say tasbih and let the women clap."
"23205","Affan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us: Abu Hazim narrated to us, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: There was fighting between Banu Amr ibn Awf, and it reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he went to them after Zuhr to make peace between them. He said: O Bilal, if the prayer comes and I have not come, then order Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer. He said: When Asr came, Bilal called the iqamah for prayer, then ordered Abu Bakr, so he stepped forward with them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came after Abu Bakr had entered the prayer. When they saw him they clapped, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came parting the people until he stood behind Abu Bakr. He said: Abu Bakr, when he entered prayer, would not turn around, but when he saw the clapping would not stop, he turned and saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) behind him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gestured to him with his hand to go ahead. Abu Bakr stood a while, then praised Allah for that, then walked backwards. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stepped forward and prayed with the people. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished his prayer, he said: O Abu Bakr, what prevented you, when I gestured to you, from going ahead? Abu Bakr said: It was not for Ibn Abi Quhafah to lead the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in prayer. He said to the people: If something befalls you in your prayer, let the men say tasbih and let the women clap."
"23206","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Paradise has a gate called al-Rayyan. He said: It will be said on the Day of Resurrection: Where are the fasting ones? Come to al-Rayyan. When the last of them enters, that gate will be closed."
"23207","Affan narrated to us: Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Paradise has a gate called al-Rayyan. It will be said on the Day of Resurrection: Where are the fasting ones? When they enter it, it will be closed, and none besides them will enter through it. He said: I met Abu Hazim and asked him, and he narrated it to me, except that I retain the hadith of Abd al-Rahman better."
"23208","Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us: Ya'qub ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I and the caretaker of the orphan are like these two in Paradise. And he pointed with the index and middle fingers, separating them slightly."
"23209","Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us: Ya'qub ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Abu Hazim: Sahl ibn Sa'd informed me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of Khaybar: I will give this banner tomorrow to a man at whose hands Allah will grant victory, who loves Allah and His Messenger, and whom Allah and His Messenger love. He said: The people spent the night debating which of them would be given it. In the morning they went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), each hoping to be given it. He said: Where is Ali ibn Abi Talib? It was said: O Messenger of Allah, he is complaining of his eyes. He said: Send for him. He was brought, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spat in his eyes and prayed for him, and he was healed until it was as if he had no pain. He gave him the banner. Ali said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I fight them until they become like us? He said: Proceed calmly until you halt in their courtyard, then call them to Islam and inform them of what is due upon them of the right of Allah therein. By Allah, for Allah to guide one man through you is better for you than for you to have red camels."
"23210","Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us: Ya'qub ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, who said: I heard Sahl saying: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I am your forerunner at the Hawd. Whoever comes to it will drink, and whoever drinks will never thirst after it. Some peoples will come to me whom I know and who know me, then a barrier will be placed between me and them. Abu Hazim said: Al-Nu'man ibn Abi Ayyash heard me while I was narrating this hadith to them, and said: Did you hear Sahl saying thus? He said: I said: Yes. He said: And I bear witness that Abu Sa'id al-Khudri added to it, saying: They are from me. It will be said: You do not know what they did after you. So I will say: Away, away with whoever changed after me."
"23211","Affan narrated to us: Umar ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever guarantees for me what is between his jaws and what is between his legs, I will guarantee Paradise for him."
"23212","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to me: Malik narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Ansari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a drink and drank from it, and on his right was a boy and on his left were the elders. He said to the boy: Will you permit me to give these? He said: No, by Allah, I will not prefer anyone over my share from you. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) thrust it into his hand."
"23213","Surayj ibn al-Nu'man narrated to us: Ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, he said: My father informed me, from Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi, that a woman came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a woven burdah containing its borders. Sahl said: Do you know what a burdah is? They said: Yes, it is a shamlah. He said: Yes. She said: O Messenger of Allah, I wove this with my hands and brought it to clothe you with it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took it, being in need of it, and came out to us wearing it as his izar. So-and-so, the son of so-and-so, a man whom he named, felt it and said: How fine this burdah is; clothe me with it, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Yes. When he entered, he folded it and sent it to him. The people said to him: By Allah, you did not do well; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was clothed with it, being in need of it, then you asked him for it, though you knew he does not turn away a asker. He said: By Allah, I did not ask him for it to wear it, but I asked him for it so it would be my shroud on the day I die. Sahl said: So it was his shroud on the day he died."
"23214","Harun ibn Ma'ruf narrated to us, and I heard it myself from Harun ibn Ma'ruf: Ibn Wahb informed us: Abu Sakhr narrated to me that Abu Hazim narrated to him, he said: I heard Sahl ibn Sa'd saying: I witnessed a gathering of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in which he described Paradise until he finished, then said at the end of his hadith: In it is what no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and has never crossed the heart of a human. Then he recited this verse: Their sides forsake their beds, they call upon their Lord in fear and hope, and they spend from what We provided them. No soul knows what is hidden for them of delight of eyes as reward for what they used to do."
"23215","Nuh ibn Maymun narrated to us: Malik informed us, from Ibn Shihab: Sahl ibn Sa'd informed me, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he disliked questions and criticized them."
"23216","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Sufyan informed us, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People will remain well as long as they hasten the iftar."
"23217","Rib'i ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, that Sahl ibn Sa'd said: I saw Fatimah, daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), on the day of Uhud burning a piece of mat, then taking it and placing it upon the wound of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on his face. He said: A shield containing water was brought, and she washed the blood from him."
"23218","Abu Kamil narrated to us: Ibrahim, meaning Ibn Sa'd, narrated to us: Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: Uwaymir came to Asim ibn Adi and said: Ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): What do you think of a man who finds a man with his wife and kills him, will he be killed for him, or how should he act? He said: So Asim asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disapproved of questions. He said: Uwaymir met him and said: What did you do? He said: You have brought me nothing good; I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he disapproved of questions. Uwaymir said: By Allah, I will come to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and ask him. So he came to him and found that revelation had come down concerning them. He said: He called for them and performed li'an between them. He said: Uwaymir said: If I take her back, O Messenger of Allah, I would have lied about her. He said: So he parted from her before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him. He said: So it became a sunnah for the mutual cursers. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Watch her; if she brings him dark, deep-black-eyed, large-buttocked, then I think he has told the truth, and if she brings him red as if a waharah, then I think he is lying. He said: She brought him in the disliked description."
"23219","Ibn Idris narrated to us: Ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi, who said: When Uwaymir, brother of Banu al-Ajlan, performed li'an against his wife, he said: O Messenger of Allah, I would wrong her if I kept her; she is divorced, she is divorced, she is divorced."
"23220","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Ma'mar narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: I heard him narrating that a woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he mentioned the hadith. He said: Do you recite anything of the Quran? He said: Yes. He said: What? He said: Such-and-such surah, and such-and-such surah, and such-and-such surah. He said: I have given her to you in marriage for what you have of the Quran. He said: I saw him going while she followed him."
"23221","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, that a man peeped at the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from behind the curtain of his chamber, while in the hand of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was a midra. He said: Had I known this one was looking at me until I reached him, I would have stabbed his eye with the midra. Has seeking permission been ordained except for the sake of sight?"
"23222","Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: I was sent, I and the Hour, like this from this."
"23223","Yazid narrated to us: Abu Ghassan Muhammad ibn Mutarrif narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man may do the deeds of the people of Hellfire, yet he is among the people of Paradise, and a man may do the deeds of the people of Paradise, yet he is among the people of Hellfire. Deeds are only by their endings."
"23224","Rawh and Isma'il ibn Umar both said: Malik narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If there is evil omen, it is in the horse, the woman, and the dwelling, meaning evil omen."
"23225","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, and Ya'qub: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq: Abbas ibn Sahl ibn Sa'd narrated to me, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Asim ibn Adi: Take her to yourself until she gives birth with you; if she bears him red, then he belongs to his father who disowned him, Uwaymir, and if she bears him curly-haired, black-tongued, then he belongs to Ibn al-Sahma'. Asim said: When it occurred, I took him to myself, and his head was like the fleece of a small lamb. Then I took, Ya'qub said, by his jaws, and he was reddish like a nabqah, and his tongue met me black like a date. He said: I said: Allah and His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spoke the truth."
"23226","Abd Allah ibn al-Harith narrated to us: al-Aslami, meaning Abd Allah ibn Amir, narrated to me, from Imran ibn Abi Anas, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the mosque founded upon piety, he said: It is my mosque."
"23227","Abd Allah narrated to us: Yahya ibn Ma'in narrated to us: Hisham ibn Yusuf narrated to us, from Ma'mar, and my father narrated to us: Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us: Hisham ibn Yusuf narrated to us: Ma'mar narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seventy thousand of my ummah will enter Paradise, or he said seven hundred thousand, without reckoning."
"23228","Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us: Mus'ab ibn Thabit narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer is affectionate, and there is no good in one who does not befriend and is not befriended."
"23229","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Mutarrif narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: My minbar is upon a tur'ah of the tur'as of Paradise. I said to him: What is a tur'ah, O Abu al-Abbas? He said: A gate."
"23230","Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi and Ishaq ibn Isa both said: Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The fasting ones have a gate in Paradise called al-Rayyan; none besides them enters through it. When the last of them enters, it will be closed. Whoever enters through it will drink, and whoever drinks from it will never thirst."
"23231","Abu Nuh narrated to us: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked questions and criticized them."
"23232","Waki' ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, and Abd al-Rahman: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A morning going or an evening going in the cause of Allah is better than the world and what is in it."
"23233","Waki' narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, and Abd al-Rahman: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Tasbih in prayer is for men, and clapping is for women."
"23234","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi and Ishaq ibn Yusuf al-Azraq both said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People will remain well as long as they hasten the iftar."
"23235","Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us: Abu Hazim narrated to us, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: We used to take a midday nap and eat lunch after Jumu'ah with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"23236","Bahz narrated to us: Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us: Abu Hazim informed us, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to Banu Amr ibn Awf concerning a dispute, meaning a quarrel between them, to make peace between them. The prayer time came, and Bilal said to Abu Bakr: Shall I call the iqamah and you lead the people? Abu Bakr said: Yes. Bilal called the iqamah and Abu Bakr stepped forward to lead the people. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came parting the rows, and the people clapped. Abu Bakr would hardly turn around in prayer, but when they increased, Abu Bakr turned and there was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) parting the rows. Abu Bakr stepped back, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gestured to him: Your place. Abu Bakr stepped back, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stepped forward and prayed with them. When he finished his prayer he said: O Abu Bakr, how was it with you, when I gestured to you, that you did not remain? He said: It was not for Ibn Abi Quhafah to lead the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is with you, that when something befalls you, you clap? Say tasbih, for clapping is for women."
"23237","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Malik, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The people were ordered to place the right hand upon the left in prayer. Abu Hazim said: I know only that he attributes that. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Attributes means raises it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"23238","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman, from Malik, and Ishaq narrated to us: Malik informed us, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, that a woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have given myself to you. She stood a long standing. A man stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, marry her to me if you have no need of her. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you have anything to give her as dowry? He said: I have nothing but this izar of mine. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you give her your izar, you will sit with no izar. Seek something. He said: I find nothing. He said: Seek, even an iron ring. He sought but found nothing. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Do you have any of the Quran with you? He said: Yes, such-and-such surah and such-and-such surah, naming surahs. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: I have married her to you for what you have of the Quran."
"23239","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman, from Malik, from Ibn Shihab, and Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us: Malik informed me, from Ibn Shihab, that Sahl ibn Sa'd informed him that Uwaymir al-Ajlani came to Asim ibn Adi al-Ansari and said: O Asim, what do you think of a man who finds a man with his wife, does he kill him so you kill him, or how should he act? Ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about that for me, O Asim. Asim asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about that, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked questions and criticized them, until what Asim heard became grave to him. Ishaq said: What he heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When Asim returned to his family, Uwaymir came to him and said: O Asim, what did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say? Asim said to Uwaymir: You brought me nothing good; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked the question you asked him about. Uwaymir said: By Allah, I will not stop until I ask him about it. Uwaymir came until he reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among the people and said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): What do you think of a man who finds a man with his wife, does he kill him so you kill him, or how should he act? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Allah has revealed concerning you and your companion, so go and bring her. Sahl ibn Sa'd said: They performed li'an while I was with the people at the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When they finished, Uwaymir said: I lied about her, O Messenger of Allah, if I keep her. So he divorced her thrice before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him."
"23240","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik, from Abu Hazim ibn Dinar, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to Banu Amr ibn Awf to make peace between them, and he mentioned the hadith. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gestured to him to remain in your place. Abu Bakr raised his hands to the sky and praised Allah for what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had ordered him of that. Then Abu Bakr stepped back until he stood level in the row, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stepped forward and prayed. He mentioned like the meaning of the hadith of Hammad ibn Salamah."
"23241","Hajjaj narrated to us: Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us: Uqayl ibn Khalid narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Sahl, that he said: A man of the Ansar came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think of a man who finds a man with his wife, does he kill him? He said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed concerning his case what is mentioned in the Quran of li'an. He said: It has been decreed for you and your wife. He said: They performed li'an while I was a witness, then he parted from her at the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"23242","Hammad ibn Khalid narrated to us: Abd Allah, meaning Ibn Umar, narrated to us, from al-Abbas ibn Sahl al-Sa'idi, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to lean against a trunk. He said: The people have increased, and would that I had something, meaning to sit upon. Abbas said: My father went and cut the minbar wood from the ghaba. He said: I do not know whether my father made it or had it made."
"23243","Rib'i ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Mu'awiyah, from Ibn Abi Dhubab, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raising his hands at all, supplicating upon a minbar or elsewhere; he would only place his hands level with his shoulders and point with his finger, a pointing."
"23244","Hashim narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz, meaning Ibn Abi Salamah, narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi, from Asim ibn Adi, who said: Uwaymir, a man of Banu Ajlan, came to him and said: O Asim, what do you think of a man who finds a man with his wife, does he kill him so they kill him, or how should he act? Ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for me, O Asim. Asim asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about that, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked questions and criticized them, until what he heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became grave to Asim. He mentioned the meaning of the hadith of Malik, except that he said: He divorced her before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him. He said: His parting from her became a sunnah for the mutual cursers."
"23245","Yunus narrated to us: al-Attaf ibn Khalid narrated to us: Abu Hazim narrated to us, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: A morning going in the cause of Allah is better than the world and what is in it, and an evening going in the cause of Allah is better than the world and what is in it, and the spot of a whip in Paradise is better than the world and what is in it."
"23246","Husayn narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Mutarrif narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: An evening going in the cause of Allah, and he mentioned its meaning."
"23247","Isma'il ibn Umar narrated to us: Malik narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People will remain well as long as they hasten the iftar."
"23248","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us: al-Fudayl, meaning Ibn Sulayman, narrated to us: Muhammad, meaning Ibn Abi Yahya, narrated to us, from his mother, who said: I heard Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi saying: I gave drink to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with my hands from Buda'ah."
"23249","Husayn, from al-Fudayl, meaning Ibn Sulayman, narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abi Yahya narrated to us, from al-Abbas ibn Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi, from his father, who said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at al-Khandaq. He took the mattock and dug with it, and struck a rock, and laughed. It was said: What makes you laugh, O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: I laughed at people who will be brought from the direction of the east in shackles, driven to Paradise."
"23250","Husayn narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Mutarrif narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I was sent, and the Hour, like this. And he pointed with his two fingers, the index and the middle."
"23251","Hujayn ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz, meaning Ibn Abi Salamah, narrated to us, from Abu Hazim al-Qass, from Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi, companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: One who came came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Banu Amr ibn Awf have fought one another and pelted with stones. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to them to make peace between them, and the prayer time came. Bilal came to Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with him, and said: Will you pray, so I call the iqamah? He said: Yes. He said: Bilal called the iqamah, and Abu Bakr stepped forward. When he entered the prayer and the people formed rows behind him, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came from where he had gone, parting the rows until he reached the first row, then stood. The people began clapping to inform Abu Bakr of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Abu Bakr would not turn around in prayer, but when they increased upon him, he turned, and there was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) behind him with the people. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gestured to him to remain firm. He raised his hands as if supplicating, then stepped back heel-first until he reached the row. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stepped forward and prayed with the people. When he finished his prayer, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is with you, that when something befell you in your prayer you began clapping? If something befalls one of you in his prayer, let him say tasbih; tasbih is for men and clapping is for women. Then he said to Abu Bakr: Why did you raise your hands? What prevented you from remaining firm when I gestured to you? He said: I raised my hands because I praised Allah for what I saw of you, and it was not fitting for Ibn Abi Quhafah to lead the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"23252","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Malik, from Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Ansari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to give taslim in his prayer to his right and his left, until the whiteness of his cheeks was seen."
"23253","Hasan narrated to us: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us: Bakr ibn Sawadah narrated to us, from Wafa ibn Shurayh al-Sadafi, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among you is the Book of Allah, learned by the black, the red, and the white. Learn it before there comes a time when people learn it and it does not pass their throats, and they straighten it as the arrow is straightened, and they hasten its reward and do not defer it."
"23254","Isma'il ibn Umar al-Wasiti narrated to us: Malik narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If evil omen is in anything, it is in the woman, the horse, and the dwelling."
"23255","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: It was read to Malik: Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a drink and drank from it, and on his right was a boy and on his left were the elders. He said to the boy: Will you permit that I give them? He said: By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I would not prefer anyone over my share from you."
"23256","Issam ibn Khalid and Abu al-Nadr both said: al-Attaf ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); Abu al-Nadr said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A morning going in the cause of Allah is better than the world and what is in it, and an evening going in the cause of Allah is better than the world and what is in it, and the spot of a whip in Paradise, Abu al-Nadr said: of Paradise, is better than the world and what is in it."
"23257","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Ghasil narrated to us, from Hamzah ibn Abi Usayd, from his father, and Abbas ibn Sahl, from his father, who both said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by us with companions of his, and we went out until we proceeded to a garden called al-Shawt. When we reached two gardens, we sat between them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sit. He entered, and al-Jawniyah was brought and set apart in a house among the palms, Umaymah bint al-Nu'man ibn Sharahil, with a midwife of hers. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon her, he said: Give yourself to me. She said: Does a queen give herself to a commoner? My father said, and other than Abu Ahmad said: A woman of Banu al-Jawn called Umaynah said: I seek refuge in Allah from you. He said: You have sought refuge in One who grants refuge. Then he came out to us and said: O Abu Usayd, clothe her with two Persian garments and join her to her family."
"23258","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us: Malik informed me, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People will remain well as long as they hasten the iftar."
"23259","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, from his father, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, that he was asked about the minbar, of what wood it was. He said: By Allah, I know of what wood it is, and I know who made it, and on what day it was made, and on what day it was placed. I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the first day he sat upon it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to a woman who had a carpenter boy, and said to her: Order your carpenter boy to make for me woods upon which I sit when I speak to the people. She ordered him, and he went to the ghaba and cut tamarisk, and made the minbar of three steps. It was sent to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and placed in this spot of his which you see. He sat upon it the first day it was placed, and uttered takbir upon it, then bowed, then descended backwards and prostrated, and the people prostrated with him. Then he returned until he finished. When he turned he said: O people, I did this so that you follow me and learn my prayer. It was said to Sahl: Was there of the matter of the trunk what the people say? He said: There was of it what there was."
"23260","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman, meaning Ibn Abd Allah ibn Dinar, narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Guarding for a day in the cause of Allah is better than the world and what is upon it. The evening outing a servant goes out in the cause of Allah, or the morning going, is better than the world and what is upon it. The spot of the whip of one of you in Paradise is better than the world and what is upon it."
"23261","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman, meaning Ibn Abd Allah ibn Dinar, narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am your forerunner at the Hawd. Whoever comes to me will drink, and whoever drinks will never thirst. I perceived that some peoples will come to me whom I know and who know me, then a barrier will be placed between me and them. He said: Al-Nu'man ibn Abi Ayyash heard me narrating it and said: And I bear witness that Abu Sa'id al-Khudri adds to it, saying: And I will say: They are my ummah, or from me. It will be said: You do not know what they innovated after you, or what they changed after you. So I will say: Away, away with whoever changed after me."
"23262","Yunus narrated to us: Imran ibn Yazid al-Qattan, a Basran, narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This minbar of mine is upon a tur'ah of the tur'as of Paradise."
"23263","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Muslim narrated to us, from Abbad ibn Ishaq, from Abu Hazim: Sahl ibn Sa'd narrated to me that a man of Aslam came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: He has committed zina with a woman, naming her. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to the woman and called her, and asked her about what he said, and she denied. So he flogged him and left her."
"23264","Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us: Ya'qub ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of Paradise will see the chamber in Paradise as you see the star in the sky. He said: I narrated that to al-Nu'man ibn Abi Ayyash, and he said: I heard Abu Sa'id al-Khudri saying: As you see the brilliant star in the eastern or western horizon."
"23265","Ahmad ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us: Abd Allah narrated to us: Mus'ab ibn Thabit informed us: Abu Hazim narrated to me, he said: I heard Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The believer among the people of faith is like the head to the body; the believer aches for the people of faith as the body aches for what is in the head."
"23266","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Ibn Lahi'ah informed us, from Bakr ibn Sawadah, from Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Ansari, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, you will surely follow the ways of those before you, example by example."
"23267","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us: Ibn Lahi'ah informed us: Jamil al-Aslami narrated to us, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, let me not reach a time, or let you not reach a time, in which the learned is not followed and the forbearing is not shy of. Their hearts are the hearts of non-Arabs and their tongues are the tongues of Arabs."
"23268","Hasan narrated to us: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us: Abu Zur'ah Amr ibn Jabir narrated to us, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Do not revile Tubba', for he had submitted."
